<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Chromecorp yr shr falls 28 pct, div held.</title>
<headline>Chromecorp yr shr falls 28 pct, div held.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)   51	   vs   71</p>
<p>    Attrib income	 94.86	vs  126.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		144.76	vs  184.37</p>
<p>    Tax		     51.89	vs   57.40</p>
<p>    Interest charge	2.57 gain vs    3.49 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover	     716.52	vs  610.19</p>
<p>Full name: Chromecorp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would retain its cash resources in order to fund its continuing expansion programme. As a result, no dividend was proposed.</p>
<p>It said that despite low product price levels, physical demand for ferrochrome had picked up, indicating that the market was nearing a balanced supply and demand situation.</p>
<p>After negative growth in stainless steel production in 1996, coupled with the severe destocking of inventories, demand for ferrochrome was expected to be fuelled by an upturn in the production of stainless steel, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
